Building the OMNeT++ documentation
==================================

The unified HTML site (manual, guides, tutorials, articles, C++ and Python API
reference) is built with Sphinx:

    $ make ci-html

The Python toolchain is managed with uv (https://docs.astral.sh/uv/): the build
runs `uv sync --frozen` to create ./.venv from the pinned uv.lock, so only uv
itself has to be installed. Native tools needed for this target, on Ubuntu:

    $ sudo apt install doxygen graphviz pandoc

Math is rendered client-side by KaTeX, so no LaTeX is required for the site.

The easiest way to reproduce the exact CI toolchain (pinned doxygen and pandoc)
is the doc-builder container image; see site/doc-builder/README.md. The whole
site build/deploy pipeline is documented in site/README.md.

Legacy targets
--------------

The legacy html, PDF and Eclipse-help outputs (`make all`, `do-manual-pdf`, `do-guides-pdf`,
`do-manual-html`, `do-manual-eclipse`) still go through LaTeX and need more:

    $ sudo apt install texlive texlive-latex-extra latexmk librsvg2-bin \
          libxml2-utils perl
